From per_render_multi_flush Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Wed, 13 May 2026 07:30:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] freedreno: A22X per-render multi-flush to align per-IB cycle
 counter (v2)

Mainline-Linux + freedreno renders the GLES2 hello-triangle on Adreno
220 with a deterministic period-16 cycle - only 1 in 16 caps produces
the bit-exact correct output.

Background

  Investigation across patches 0090..0098 (Fork A/B HW binning,
  CP_SET_BIN_DATA visibility consume, SQ slot scrub, kernel hw_init
  pulses) localised the cycle to GPU-internal state below the MMIO
  interface.

  On 2026-05-13 we booted the device to stock webOS and ran
  tools/gpu-regdump/gl-cap-and-regdump-webos under strace.  webOS
  issues EXACTLY 16 IOCTL_KGSL_RINGBUFFER_ISSUEIBCMDS per render on
  /dev/kgsl-3d0.  Mainline Mesa freedreno's Fork A/B path issues 1
  ioctl per render (the entire per-tile loop is built into a single
  ringbuffer and submitted in one MSM_SUBMIT).

  v9 0099 NOP-IB sweep (kernel repo reports/v9-nop-ib-sweep-2026-
  05-13.md) falsified the per-CP_INDIRECT_BUFFER hypothesis: adding
  0..30 NOP CP_INDIRECT_BUFFER calls inside one Mesa submit produced
  IDENTICAL cycles.  The GPU's state-cycle counter advances per
  ISSUEIBCMDS (per Mesa flush), NOT per IB call inside one submit.
  Period is 16, advance is +1 per Mesa flush, counter resets to
  phase 0 on kernel boot.

  webOS's 16 ioctls/render -> 16 advances -> wrap mod-16 -> no
  visible cycle.  Mainline's 1 ioctl/render -> walks all 16 phases
  over 16 consecutive renders.

v10 v1 failure mode (2026-05-13)

  First implementation used a bare 2-dword CP_NOP ringbuffer per
  dummy submit AND never called fd_ringbuffer_del() before
  fd_submit_del() (the freedreno_ringbuffer.h contract says "all
  ringbuffer's create from the submit should be unref'd before
  destroying the submit").  On fresh-boot the very first dummy
  submit hung the GPU at every multiplier >= 2 (80 hangchecks
  across 4 multipliers, 5 caps each).

  Two suspected causes:
    1. Leaked ringbuffer refs leave BO state in flight.
    2. Bare CP_NOP IB1 may not be enough work for the kernel /
       CP_INDIRECT_BRANCH wrapper - other freedreno submit paths
       always include at least a CP_EVENT_WRITE for fence/cache
       coherency.

v2 fix

  Three changes vs v1:

    a) Call fd_ringbuffer_del(rb) before fd_submit_del(dummy),
       honouring the freedreno_ringbuffer.h lifecycle contract.

    b) Replace the 2-dword CP_NOP with a 4-dword body:
         CP_EVENT_WRITE CACHE_FLUSH_AND_INV_EVENT  (2 dwords)
         CP_NOP 0x00000000                          (2 dwords)
       The CACHE_FLUSH_AND_INV_EVENT (0x16 A2XX-specific) is the
       same event fd2_emit_tile_renderprep emits for A22X mem2gmem
       coherency - proven safe on this HW.  Adds a real work item
       for the CP to retire so the dummy submit's RB->IB1->RB
       sequence has meaningful content.

    c) Larger initial RB allocation (32 bytes / 8 dwords) so the
       allocator has headroom for any kernel-side prologue that
       fd_submit_flush may prepend.

  Just before the real fd_submit_flush() in
  freedreno_gmem.c::flush_ring(), inject (multiplier - 1) such
  dummy fd_submit_flush() calls.  Each dummy is its own MSM_SUBMIT
  -> own ISSUEIBCMDS equivalent -> +1 GPU counter advance.

  Total submits per Mesa render = multiplier (default 16) ->
  counter advance per render = 16 mod 16 = 0 -> cycle phase
  pinned at the kernel-boot value (phase 0 = 5adc3160 = correct
  clean RGB triangle).

  Tunable via env-var FD2_FLUSH_MULTIPLIER=<n>:
    n=0/1 -> control / disable (period-16 cycle reappears)
    n=2   -> period-8 cycle (1 in 8 correct)
    n=8   -> period-2 cycle (every other cap correct)
    n=16  -> default, cycle collapsed to single phase
    n=32  -> two full wraps, still single phase

  Only fires for is_a22x(screen).  A20X / A3XX / A4XX / etc.
  untouched.

  Cost: 15 extra MSM_SUBMIT ioctls per real render (~10-100 us each
  at A22X kernel-ioctl rate, worst case ~1.5 ms extra per frame),
  plus 15 extra CACHE_FLUSH_AND_INV_EVENT (the same event already
  emitted by fd2_emit_tile_renderprep, no new side effect).

  No persistent state: each dummy submit builds + flushes + frees
  inline.

Expected test outcome

  Fresh-boot 16-cap default test post-deploy: all 16 caps should
  produce 5adc3160 (correct RGB triangle), 0 hangchecks.

  Bisect via FD2_FLUSH_MULTIPLIER:
    FD2_FLUSH_MULTIPLIER=1  -> reverts to period-16 cycle (control)
    FD2_FLUSH_MULTIPLIER=2  -> period-8 cycle
    FD2_FLUSH_MULTIPLIER=8  -> period-2 cycle
    FD2_FLUSH_MULTIPLIER=16 -> all 5adc3160

  If v2 still hangs, the dummy-submit construction itself is wrong
  even with cache-flush body - next pivot would be post-submit
  injection (move dummies to AFTER the real submit) or per-tile
  split (architectural match to webOS, much more invasive).

Upstream-Status: Pending

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
---
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/freedreno_gmem.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/freedreno_gmem.c
@@ -670,6 +670,99 @@
       ctx->emit_sysmem_fini(batch);
 }

+/* v10 0099 v2: A22X per-IB cycle-counter alignment via multi-flush.
+ *
+ * The Adreno 220 has an internal state-cycle counter that advances by
+ * exactly +1 per IOCTL_KGSL_RINGBUFFER_ISSUEIBCMDS (= per Mesa
+ * fd_submit_flush()), period 16.  webOS strace (2026-05-13, kernel
+ * repo reports/webos-strace-2026-05-13/) shows webOS's libGLESv2
+ * issues 16 such ioctls per render, wrapping the counter to phase 0
+ * every render and producing no visible cycle.  Mainline Mesa
+ * freedreno's Fork A/B path emits exactly one ioctl per render (the
+ * per-tile loop is built into a single ringbuffer), so the counter
+ * advances +1/render -> walks all 16 phases over 16 consecutive
+ * renders -> visible period-16 cycle of complete frames where only
+ * 1 in 16 caps (5adc3160) is bit-exact correct.
+ *
+ * v1 (bare CP_NOP, no ringbuffer del) hung first dummy submit at
+ * every multiplier >= 2 from fresh boot.  v2 honours the
+ * fd_ringbuffer lifecycle contract AND gives the dummy a real CP
+ * work item (CACHE_FLUSH_AND_INV_EVENT, same A22X event already
+ * emitted by fd2_emit_tile_renderprep).
+ *
+ * Fix: just before the real fd_submit_flush, issue (multiplier - 1)
+ * dummy fd_submit_flush() calls.  Each dummy ringbuffer contains:
+ *   CP_EVENT_WRITE CACHE_FLUSH_AND_INV_EVENT   (2 dwords)
+ *   CP_NOP 0x00000000                           (2 dwords)
+ * for a total 4-dword IB1.  Each dummy is its own MSM_SUBMIT ->
+ * +1 counter advance.  Total submits per render = multiplier
+ * (default 16) -> counter advance per render = 16 mod 16 = 0 ->
+ * cycle wraps to a fixed phase every render.  GPU counter resets
+ * to phase 0 on kernel boot, so all renders post-boot land at
+ * phase 0 -> 5adc3160 (correct) every cap.
+ *
+ * Tunable via env-var FD2_FLUSH_MULTIPLIER=<n>:
+ *   n=0/1 -> control / disable (period-16 cycle reappears)
+ *   n=2   -> period-8 cycle (1 in 8 correct)
+ *   n=8   -> period-2 cycle (every other cap correct)
+ *   n=16  -> default, cycle collapsed to single phase
+ *   n=32  -> two full wraps, still single phase
+ *
+ * Only fires for is_a22x(screen).  A20X / future Adreno gens
+ * untouched.  Cost: 15 extra MSM_SUBMIT ioctls per real render
+ * (~10-100 us each at A22X kernel-ioctl rate, worst case ~1.5 ms
+ * extra per frame).
+ *
+ * CACHE_FLUSH_AND_INV_EVENT value 0x16 is A2XX-specific
+ * (registers/adreno/adreno_pm4.xml: <value name="CACHE_FLUSH_AND_
+ * INV_EVENT" value="0x16" variants="A2XX"/>).
+ */
+static void
+fd_a22x_multi_flush_align(struct fd_batch *batch)
+{
+   struct fd_screen *screen = batch->ctx->screen;
+
+   if (FD_DBG(NOHW))
+      return;
+   if (!is_a22x(screen))
+      return;
+
+   int multiplier = 16;
+   const char *e = getenv("FD2_FLUSH_MULTIPLIER");
+   if (e)
+      multiplier = atoi(e);
+   if (multiplier <= 1)
+      return;
+
+   for (int i = 0; i < multiplier - 1; i++) {
+      struct fd_submit *dummy = fd_submit_new(batch->ctx->pipe);
+      if (!dummy)
+         break;
+      struct fd_ringbuffer *rb =
+         fd_submit_new_ringbuffer(dummy, 32, FD_RINGBUFFER_PRIMARY);
+      if (!rb) {
+         fd_submit_del(dummy);
+         break;
+      }
+      /* CACHE_FLUSH_AND_INV_EVENT (A2XX, 0x16): same event the A22X
+       * mem2gmem path in fd2_emit_tile_renderprep emits for coherency.
+       * Gives the dummy IB1 a real work item the CP can retire. */
+      OUT_PKT3(rb, CP_EVENT_WRITE, 1);
+      OUT_RING(rb, 0x16);  /* CACHE_FLUSH_AND_INV_EVENT */
+      OUT_PKT3(rb, CP_NOP, 0);
+      OUT_RING(rb, 0x00000000);
+
+      struct fd_fence *df = fd_submit_flush(dummy, -1, false);
+      if (df)
+         fd_fence_del(df);
+
+      /* freedreno_ringbuffer.h: all rb's must be unref'd before
+       * fd_submit_del.  v1 violated this -> first-dummy hang. */
+      fd_ringbuffer_del(rb);
+      fd_submit_del(dummy);
+   }
+}
+
 static void
 flush_ring(struct fd_batch *batch)
 {
@@ -679,6 +772,12 @@

    struct fd_fence *fence;

+   /* v10 0099 v2: align A22X per-IB cycle counter to phase 0 with
+    * N-1 dummy ISSUEIBCMDS before the real submit.  See block comment
+    * above fd_a22x_multi_flush_align() for full rationale.
+    */
+   fd_a22x_multi_flush_align(batch);
+
    if (FD_DBG(NOHW)) {
       /* construct a dummy fence: */
       fence = fd_fence_new(batch->ctx->pipe, use_fence_fd);
